    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a computed `displayName` field, formatted `LastName, FirstName`, to owner responses.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped it via a small single-purpose helper:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\n   default String displayName(Owner owner) {\n       return owner == null ? null : owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName();\n   }\n   ```\n\nBecause the responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated` and the GET path's `RespondWithOwner`) both go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the field is populated from the stored names on both create and read \u2014 no changes needed to the OfficeFloor pipeline itself.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
